---
layout: article
title: Resource scopes
description: Learn how Appwrite Firewall scopes rules to the project API, a Function, or a Site, and where each scope is enforced.
---

Every Firewall rule has a **resource type** that limits which traffic the rule can match. Scopes keep API-wide policies separate from policies for a single function or site.

# Scope types {% #scope-types %}

| Resource type | Applies to | Resource ID |
|---------------|------------|-------------|
| **API** | Project Appwrite API traffic (`/v1/...`) | Not required (stored empty) |
| **Functions** | Public/edge traffic for one function | Function ID required |
| **Sites** | Public/edge traffic for one site | Site ID required |

# Where rules are enforced {% #where-rules-are-enforced %}

- **API** rules are enforced on requests to your project's Appwrite API. This is the scope to use for Auth, Databases, Storage, and other `/v1` services.
- **Functions** and **Sites** rules are stored on the project and applied to that function's or site's **public traffic** on the Appwrite Network edge.
- Function and site rules do **not** block Console or Appwrite **management API** calls used to create, update, or deploy those resources. A deny rule on a function will not stop `GET /v1/functions/{id}` from a valid API key or the Console.

{% info title="Pick the right scope" %}
To protect SDK and client calls into Appwrite services, use **API**. To protect a deployed function URL or site hostname, use **Functions** or **Sites** with that resource selected.
{% /info %}

# When to use API {% #when-to-use-api %}

Use **API** for project-wide API controls:

- Block abusive client IPs across Auth, Databases, Storage, and other API services
- Rate limit a shared path prefix such as `/v1`
- Deny traffic from specific countries for the whole project API

# When to use Functions {% #when-to-use-functions %}

Use **Functions** when only one function's public traffic should be protected or exempted:

- Rate limit a public webhook function
- Deny non-`POST` methods on an HTTP-triggered function endpoint
- Bypass Firewall checks for a trusted caller IP on that function only

Select the function in the create wizard. The rule appears when that function is selected in the resource selector.

# When to use Sites {% #when-to-use-sites %}

Use **Sites** for a single deployed web app's public traffic:

- Redirect a deprecated path on one site
- Deny admin paths on a marketing site
- Rate limit form submission paths for one site

Select the site in the create wizard. The rule appears when that site is selected in the resource selector.

# Resource selector in the Console {% #resource-selector-in-the-console %}

{% only_dark %}
![Firewall resource selector with API and site scopes](/images/docs/firewall/dark/resource-selector.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Firewall resource selector with API and site scopes](/images/docs/firewall/resource-selector.avif)
{% /only_light %}

The Firewall page filters the rules list with a resource selector. The **Project** group holds the **API** scope, and each function and site appears under its own group. Creating a rule while a function or site is selected preselects that resource in the wizard. You can change the resource type in the create wizard, or later from the rule's **Update** action.

